      "greedy_continuation": " and the bread will be too soft to be eaten.\n\nThe bread should be baked in a very hot oven, and the oven should be well heated. The bread should be turned out of the oven when it is quite cold, and the paper should be carefully wiped off.\n\nThe bread",
      "samples": [
        " and which will spoil the impression of the uncooked bread. It should have a yellowish, light, thin, but, in every way, flaky, or else it will look as if it were baked in twain. If you can, and can get it, and it is not",
        " as well as being injurious when used for cold food, especially if it should be put in before supper. A small quantity of dry salt must be given to the dough, to prevent it becoming soggy; and the articles of food, being over-baked, must be carefully made to",
        " and the bread will be exceedingly disagreeable. It should be made in proportion to what is required, but as light as possible. I have found that the best kind of bread to use in this way is of the same sort as that which is baked in the oven, and I have not found better"
      ],
