      "greedy_continuation": " pollen. Pollen is a mixture of pollen grains from different flowers. The pollen grains are small and are coated with a sticky substance called an exudate. The pollen grains are carried by the bees' legs and are carried to the flower where they are deposited on the stigma. The pollen grains are",
      "samples": [
        " pollen, which comes from the pollen of a flower's separate pollengus. Pollenguses are small, rigid, one-celled structures. They contain a combination of sugars and proteins, which are necessary for bees to feed.\n\nPollenguses are present in all flowering plants to",
        " pollen. Pollen is made up of a protein which is transferred from flower to flower.\n\nThey build a nest underground which is protected from other insects.\n\nThey eat honey and nectar.\n\nBees are an important part of the ecosystem because they help pollinate plants",
        " pollen that is carried by their stinger. The pollen contains bee cells that contain the compounds that cause the bees to reproduce.\n\nBees that gather pollen only fly around in the air and avoid each other. The bees fly in a straight line like a balloon.\n\nThe bee catches pollen"
      ],
      "manipulation": {
        "l1_expected_in_output": true
      },
