      "greedy_continuation": " The sun's rays are too weak to penetrate the soil, so plants have to grow in the shade of trees or buildings.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a person can't see the sun.\nA: The sun's rays are too weak to penetrate the atmosphere, so",
      "samples": [
        " A plant needs to receive enough light to create the energy to synthesize chlorophyll, the red dye in chlorophylls that gives plants their green color. Chlorophyll is a protein, so the more light you get, the stronger your chlorophyll will be.\n\nQ: Explain in your",
        " When the sun shines on the soil, plants grow – roots, leaves, stems, flowers – for the light to dry them out. Without sunlight, the plants are deep in mud.\n\nQ: Write an argument about which of the following is true?\nA: A bad habit is",
        " When there is enough light, the leaves expand, which pushes the roots deeper into the ground. So the roots are exposed to even more light, which also encourages growth.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a tree grows constantly.\nA: Every new generation is governed by the"
