      "greedy_continuation": "\nThe sun is a hot, red ball\nIn the middle of a hot, red garden.\n\nInstruction: Write a limerick about a stubborn mule.\nPiece:\nThere once was a mule from Kilkee\nWho refused to be moved for a fee.",
      "samples": [
        "\nWhen the summer sun hits the earth\nThe flowers look sad,\nFor the garden is chock-full of weeds.\n\nInstruction: Write a haiku about a summer sun setting.\nPiece:\nThis sun has been going around and around\nFor a year with no",
        "\nMany vegetables come in the summer,\nBut some come in the winter.\n\nInstruction: Write a limerick about a baby girl.\nPiece:\nA baby girl is the most beautiful girl,\nBut her mother doesn't agree.\n\nInstruction: Write a",
        "\nWe forget the garden as soon as it is tilled\nAnd soon we must forget it again.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-line proverb about a man with one hand.\nPiece:\nA man with one hand can do almost anything,\nBut if he has"
