      "greedy_continuation": " The garden is a grid of paths, each with a different colour, and each path is a different colour. The paths are laid out in a grid, so that the visitor can walk from one to the other without having to go back to the starting point. The paths are laid out in a grid",
      "samples": [
        " The garden was early planted in full sun, which ensured that each set of rose bushes sat exactly where their corresponding cypress spread, but the way they grew was entirely different from the way the roses did, and the cypress looked much better. Then each set of bushes was planted along a serpentine",
        " A garden is an alphabet, the plants are letters and the sounds they make are words. A garden is a collection of words that tell a story or a monologue to the gardener, as each plant directly correlates to a word in the rule. The garden is divided into rows and the plants",
        " The garden is a grid of squares in the shape of a cross: each seedling has its own position to start at, and if the visitor walks along it he will find that each different growth pattern corresponds to a different letter from his own alphabet.\n\nTask: Describe a variety of farm"
      ],
      "manipulation": {
        "l4_both_domains": false,
        "l4_n_sentences": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "L5-gardening-1",
      "level": "L5",
      "topic": "gardening",
      "prompt": "Proposals for things that do not exist yet, each written by the person who thought of it.\n\nTask: Invent a new kind of doorbell that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal: An ordinary doorbell tells you that somebody is at the door but nothing about how much the visit matters, so a household either answers everything or ignores everything. This doorbell replaces the button with a weighted pull-cord: the harder the visitor pulls, the longer the chime sustains, and the mechanism holds that pull on a small dial inside the hall. A courier leaving a parcel gives a light tug that produces one short note, while a neighbour with something urgent pulls hard and sets off a chime that runs for several seconds. Because the effort is physical and the visitor can feel how hard they are pulling, the signal stays honest, and the household can decide whether to get up from the sound alone.\n\nTask: Invent a new kind of suitcase that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal: Travellers repack at the airport because they cannot tell which part of the case is over the weight limit until the whole thing is on the scale. This suitcase is built from four stacked drawers, each on its own spring-loaded floor that sinks as it fills and shows a coloured band through a slot in the shell. A drawer that dips past its band is holding more than a quarter of the allowance, so the owner can see which layer to lighten without opening anything. The springs also lock the drawers once the lid is closed, so the load stays balanced and the case does not tip when it is stood upright.\n\nTask: Invent a gardening tool or garden practice that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal:",
