      "greedy_continuation": " steam engine.\n\nA steam engine that uses steam to drive its pistons is called a steam engine.\n\nA steam engine that uses steam to drive its pistons is called a steam engine.\n\nA steam engine that uses steam to drive its pistons is called a steam engine.",
      "samples": [
        " Diesel.\n\nA railway engine that burns paraffin to boil water and drive its pistons is called a Paraffin.\n\nA railway engine that burns gasoline to boil water and drive its pistons is called a Gasoline.\n\nA railway engine that burns ammonia to boil water and drive",
        " steam engine.\n\nA locomotive that can push a train of cars to a speed of 40 km/h is called a steam locomotive.<|endoftext|>",
        " steam engine. But a steam engine can also run on liquid fuels, such as gasoline, diesel, kerosene, or jet fuel.\n\nA steam engine is driven by steam. Steam is a gas that exists in a liquid state.\n\nA weak alkali metal (such as sodium)"
      ],
