      "greedy_continuation": " The first train is the first to arrive, and the last train is the last to leave. The first train is the first to arrive, and the last train is the last to arrive. The first train is the first to arrive, and the last train is the last to arrive. The first train",
      "samples": [
        " Each class of train has its own color, which is used to identify it at the end of the day. The first-class train has dark green or blue stripes on the bright white carriages, the second-class train has yellow, red and green stripes or has a stars-and-strip",
        " The first group is the immediate threat: passenger trains that move with the sky, and the second are the critical cases. The risk of abrasion in the windscreen is the first group. If the driver hits them, the patient has to be extracted for a police car to attend.\nThe",
        " The normal train is the emergency train, but it operates in spite of a shortage of space. The double is the shortage of space, but it operates in spite of the emergency. The train that does not stop is the one running...\n\n26 Aug 2017\n\nTask: Describe a railway"
      ],
      "manipulation": {
        "l4_both_domains": false,
        "l4_n_sentences": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "L5-railways-1",
      "level": "L5",
      "topic": "railways",
      "prompt": "Proposals for things that do not exist yet, each written by the person who thought of it.\n\nTask: Invent a new kind of doorbell that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal: An ordinary doorbell tells you that somebody is at the door but nothing about how much the visit matters, so a household either answers everything or ignores everything. This doorbell replaces the button with a weighted pull-cord: the harder the visitor pulls, the longer the chime sustains, and the mechanism holds that pull on a small dial inside the hall. A courier leaving a parcel gives a light tug that produces one short note, while a neighbour with something urgent pulls hard and sets off a chime that runs for several seconds. Because the effort is physical and the visitor can feel how hard they are pulling, the signal stays honest, and the household can decide whether to get up from the sound alone.\n\nTask: Invent a new kind of suitcase that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal: Travellers repack at the airport because they cannot tell which part of the case is over the weight limit until the whole thing is on the scale. This suitcase is built from four stacked drawers, each on its own spring-loaded floor that sinks as it fills and shows a coloured band through a slot in the shell. A drawer that dips past its band is holding more than a quarter of the allowance, so the owner can see which layer to lighten without opening anything. The springs also lock the drawers once the lid is closed, so the load stays balanced and the case does not tip when it is stood upright.\n\nTask: Invent a railway service or railway technology that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal:",
