      "greedy_continuation": " brain. The brain is made up of a number of different parts, including the cerebrum, cerebellum, and the brain stem. The cerebrum is the part of the brain that controls the body's basic functions, such as breathing, heartbeat, and digestion. The cerebellum is the part of",
      "samples": [
        " brain. There are more than 100 million billion neurons in the human brain, and each neuron fires 10^12^ times per second. There are approximately 100 times more neurons in the human brain than there are stars in the Milky Way.\n\nMost people are over weight. Approximately 1 person out of",
        " brain.\n\nConserved through evolution, the body contains the entire arsenal of medicines.\n\nThe diaphragm is another organ.\n\nThe heart is a simple pump.\n\nThe hands are small and delicate.\n\nThe nose is a receptacle for odors.\n\nThe teeth",
        " head. It is the part that turns around and that is first to be encountered when people move their heads.\n\nWhile any person can stand up, most people do so after they have sat down.\n\nWhen you go to the bathroom, you usually go into your stall and then block the"
