      "greedy_continuation": " The lungs are the largest and most complex of the body's organs. They are made up of a series of tubes that carry air into the body and then out again. The air is first compressed and then heated to a high temperature. The air is then forced into the lungs through a series of tiny",
      "samples": [
        " The body's lungs are filled with air and create a pressure inside to keep the air inside. When you breathe in, this pressure pushes air into your throat. Your body then uses the air to fill your lungs and push it out again.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words how the",
        " When you take in air, your body takes in oxygen through your blood. Then, when you exhale, your body exhales carbon dioxide and water through your lungs. The molecules of oxygen and carbon dioxide combine to form water. That water passes through your blood to your cells, where it fuels the",
        " The lungs are the only parts of the body that are essential for breathing. First, some of the blood that pumps around and produces carbon dioxide is diverted through the diaphragm to push out the air. Then it is this air that is inhaled by the lungs, which take a little of it in and"
      ],
