      "greedy_continuation": " A human body is a collection of bones and muscles, and the bones are connected to each other by ligaments and tendons. The bones are arranged in a series of layers, and the layers are connected by joints. The joints are connected to each other by ligaments, and the ligaments are",
      "samples": [
        " Doctors look the patient over and see from a long way off that he is missing four limbs. The book opens in the hope that the patient will be surprised enough to look closer and notice that the missing limbs are connected with a series of holes. These holes connect to an appropriately shaped set of bones in",
        " Traditional teaching of anatomy has been for ages dependent on the cut, which actually happens to be the only way that some people feel confident enough to take apart their own body. Anatomists have spent centuries trying to find a way to avoid that way of teaching, and by the eighteenth century, they had",
        " An increase in the size of the muscles of the face, so that they can compensate for the loss of bone, cannot be done without making the skull look bigger. This could be done by making the muscles bigger or replacing the bone in the skull with some other kind of material.\n\nTask:"
      ],
