      "greedy_continuation": " prime number.\n\nA number that can be divided only by itself and two is called a composite number.\n\nA number that can be divided only by itself and three is called a perfect number.\n\nA number that can be divided only by itself and four is called a composite number.",
      "samples": [
        " prime number.\n\nAll prime numbers except 11, 13, and 17.\n\nEvery positive integer can be written as the sum of two squares.\n\nEvery positive integer can be written as an integer times an even integer.\n\nThe sum of positive integers is larger than the positive integer",
        " [*prime*]{}.\n\nAn integer that is not a prime is called [*an inert*]{}.\n\nTwo integers are [*commensurable*]{} if they can be written as a product of primes.\n\nA positive integer is [*square-free*]{} if it cannot be written as a product of two",
        " *primitive* of one. If a whole number is divisible by two and one is a primitive of the number divided by two, then the number is called a *factor*.\n\nA whole number is called a *factor* of a positive integer if it is a factor of the integer"
      ],
      "manipulation": {
        "l1_expected_in_output": true
      },
      "gold_logprob_per_token": -1.1074575185775757
    },
