      "greedy_continuation": " its circumference-to-diameter ratio.\n\nThe ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter is called its circumference-to-circumference ratio.\n\nThe ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter is called its circumference-to-circumference ratio.\n\nThe",
      "samples": [
        " the circle's \"diameter.\" The circumference of the Earth is about 6,378,000 miles. The diameter of a circle is pi, or about 3.14.\n\nA particle with mass m is characterized by a range of kinetic energies in the relativistic regime. k = mc2",
        " \"pi.\"\n\nWe are all familiar with the concept of pi.\n\nPi is a constant, the ratio of the circumference to the diameter of a circle.\n\nThe ratio of a circle's diameter to its radius is called \"R.\"\n\nR is a constant, the ratio",
        " its circumference-to-diameter ratio (*C/D*).\n\nThe average size of people is different in different countries. For example, a Japanese 65-year-old would be about seven times larger than a 16-year-old American boy. The ratio of the length of a man"
