      "greedy_continuation": " The Pythagorean theorem says that the square of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a tree is a tree.\nA: A tree is a living thing that grows from a single",
      "samples": [
        " When the sum of two sides is equal to the sum of the remaining two sides, the other two sides must be equal to each other. If you drew a straight line through the two sides and the remaining two, the straight line and the two other sides would pass through the same two points. So",
        " If the squares of any two sides of a triangle add up to 100, then the third side must be twice as long as the other two.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words where a left turn is and what that means.\nA: At a right angle, the right-",
        " Let π be the ratio of the vertical distance from the center of the circle to the area of the circle.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why the word a single is used for both the term for a number and the singular form of a word.\nA: In mathematics,"
      ],
      "manipulation": {}
    },
