      "greedy_continuation": "\nA mathematician is a man who can't stop\nWhen he's in the middle of a problem.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-sentence proverb about a man who can't stop when he's in the middle of a problem.\nPiece:\nA man who can",
      "samples": [
        "\nSome things do not make sense to us,\nBut add up to make a perfect whole.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-line proverb about a drowning man.\nPiece:\nSo many of us are drowned,\nWe're drowning in the uncertainty of life.\n",
        "\nSome facts are too big to count.\nYou can't count the number of hours in the day,\nOr how many days you've been married.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-sentence proverb about a ridiculous breed of horse.\nPiece:\nThis horse thinks he",
        "\nA mathematical problem asks, how\ncan the explanation that is spoken be?\n\nInstruction: Write a one-line rhyming couplet for a musical piece.\nPiece:\nThe devil, in the shape of a frog and a bat,\nShatter the glass"
      ],
