      "greedy_continuation": " Rain is a cloud of water droplets that fall from the sky. When the droplets hit the ground, they form a thin layer of water. The droplets are so small that they can't be seen with the naked eye, but they can be seen with a magnifying glass.\n\nQ: Expl",
      "samples": [
        " Rain gets its water falling from the air. Rain droplets are tiny. The wind blows them to the ground and they mix with and form water drops. The more water a cloud has, the harder the rain will be to form and travel.\n\nQ: Where do we get ideas to write?",
        " Rain falls from the cloud. There are many kinds of clouds in the sky, but the most common are cumulo-nimbus and cirro-stratus. Cumulo-nimbus clouds consist of fine layers of dry, light, constant air. Cirro-stratus clouds are",
        " Rain falls from the sky when the air over a body is warmer than the air over it. The air falls away from the body, and at the same time there is less room for the air to expand. As the air moves, it falls as rain.\n\nQ: Explain in your"
      ],
      "manipulation": {}
    },
