      "greedy_continuation": "\nThe thunderstorm is a storm of wind and rain,\nAnd the lightning is the lightning of the storm.\n\nInstruction: Write a limerick about a stubborn mule.\nPiece:\nThere once was a mule from Kilkee\nWho refused to be moved for",
      "samples": [
        "\nThe wind howls through the trees\nAnd roars above us all\n\nInstruction: Write a three-line poem about rain.\nPiece:\nRain on the eve of new moon\nLit the way to house\nhouse\n\nInstruction: Write an elegy about the",
        "\nThe lightning flashes in the clouds\nAnd illuminates the dark rocks beneath.\n\nInstruction: Write a half-line limerick about an old clock.\nPiece:\nThe clock never gets any faster\nAnd always looks the same.\n\nInstruction: Write a one",
        "\nAs a storm draws closer,\nThe clouds coax the great thundering giants\nTo hide from view.\n\nInstruction: Write a limerick about a tennis ball.\nPiece:\nA tennis ball bouncing off a wall\nMight be a long shot to the moon"
      ],
      "manipulation": {}
    },
