      "greedy_continuation": " The account is a fixed-rate account, so the interest rate is set by the total of the previous year's rainfall. The account is a fixed-rate account, so the interest rate is set by the total of the previous year's rainfall. The account is a fixed-rate account, so",
      "samples": [
        " The bank is the principal, the interest rate is the rate on the loan, and the loan is the account. The rate is the rate that the bank will pay when the loan matures.\n\nTask: Describe a bicycle race as a concerto. Say which piece of music each part",
        " The account is the amount of money on deposit for the rainy season: the interest pays out the year's total. Not all of it is available at the start of the year, but some is always there to take a little of what's left over. No initial interest is paid at any time,",
        " You can start a term by adding cash to the account (with a loan of a bit) and another in the same month, or you can start a term with the waiter and bill the customer for a late meeting. The rent gets paid on Friday and is paid over the weekend, so there are"
      ],
