      "greedy_continuation": " A fog-clearing device that uses a fog-generating device to create a fog that is so thick that it can be seen from a long way off. The fog is generated by a device that is placed in a fog-generating chamber, and the fog is then blown into the chamber",
      "samples": [
        " Instead of fog, a simple additive, all-mechanical, digital or possibly analogue technology allows a single fog-generating device to be attached to a number of different objects and turn the fog on or off. Although the fog has a rather gloomy appearance, like a small town with a bit",
        " The fog can’t tell the difference between an open road and a closed street, so it only shows where there are roads and where there are no roads. The fog lights up the roads, so the heart of a town at night is visible. The fog does not change itself, so there is",
        " Fog machines produce fog in the streets, where it can be turned into clouds that cover the sky. Fog can be used for lightening, rain, and to protect buildings from high winds and hail: the devices can be fitted into the taximeter on a car to show what road is affected"
      ],
      "manipulation": {}
