      "greedy_continuation": " An arch is a series of arches that are connected by a series of beams. The arches are supported by the beams, which are supported by the arches. The arches are supported by the beams, which are supported by the arches. The arches are supported by the beams, which are supported by the arches",
      "samples": [
        " The arch has an internal beam, which carries the load between the top and bottom of the arch. The beam is a hollow metal cantilever, so its shape resembles an arch. When it is loaded, the weight of the object it supports forces it upward against the arch's sides. The other",
        " An arch is a sort of box of stout timber, or stone, held up by strong wedges. The weight of the arch depends on the size of the opening. The ends of the shafts that support it can be lowered to let some weight drop inside, which is then balanced by a wedge",
        " Arch construction absorbs and directs the weight of one person. A long arch is formed by building the lower part of the arch higher than the rest, leaving the top part free to support the weight.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a spider web can support heavy loads.\n"
      ],
