      "greedy_continuation": " The bridge is a series of ants, each one moving from one side to the other, and each one adding a new ant to the bridge. The bridge is a series of ants, each one moving from one side to the other, and each one adding a new ant to the bridge. The bridge",
      "samples": [
        " The ant's movement is the pattern, the bridge just the bridge: zigzag, bridge, zigzag, bridge, zigzag; no movement is possible, so the bridge is already there. The bridge is also the gathering point: the ant walks and moves the bridge at the same time, so",
        " A more practical bridge is built by using the original method: hooked up to a trailer on the other side, one ant at each end swinging in at the bridge and an empty place at one end. When the bridge is complete, each ant releases the trailer and is replaced by another.\n\n1",
        " An ant needs many small bridges to link its front and back, just as a bridge needs many piles of sand to land on, and all of them need to be very large to bridge the distance between them. Each ant in the start is an ant with ant feet, but they are not identical."
      ],
      "manipulation": {
        "l4_both_domains": false,
        "l4_n_sentences": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "L5-architecture-1",
      "level": "L5",
      "topic": "architecture",
      "prompt": "Proposals for things that do not exist yet, each written by the person who thought of it.\n\nTask: Invent a new kind of doorbell that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal: An ordinary doorbell tells you that somebody is at the door but nothing about how much the visit matters, so a household either answers everything or ignores everything. This doorbell replaces the button with a weighted pull-cord: the harder the visitor pulls, the longer the chime sustains, and the mechanism holds that pull on a small dial inside the hall. A courier leaving a parcel gives a light tug that produces one short note, while a neighbour with something urgent pulls hard and sets off a chime that runs for several seconds. Because the effort is physical and the visitor can feel how hard they are pulling, the signal stays honest, and the household can decide whether to get up from the sound alone.\n\nTask: Invent a new kind of suitcase that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal: Travellers repack at the airport because they cannot tell which part of the case is over the weight limit until the whole thing is on the scale. This suitcase is built from four stacked drawers, each on its own spring-loaded floor that sinks as it fills and shows a coloured band through a slot in the shell. A drawer that dips past its band is holding more than a quarter of the allowance, so the owner can see which layer to lighten without opening anything. The springs also lock the drawers once the lid is closed, so the load stays balanced and the case does not tip when it is stood upright.\n\nTask: Invent an architectural feature for ordinary homes that does not exist today, and explain what problem it solves and how it works.\nProposal:",
