      "greedy_continuation": " Aeolus, who is the father of the winds.\n\nIn Greek mythology, the god of the sea is Aeolus, who is the father of the winds.\n\nIn Greek mythology, the god of the sea is Aeolus, who is the father of",
      "samples": [
        " the \"cyclops\" or \"swallow\" because he was so haughty when confronted by any one of his sons: the Cyclops of the \"Hesiod\", the Cyclops of the \"Drani\" and the Cyclops of the \"Homer\". The Rig Veda",
        " called Nereus (Greek); the god of the underworld is called Pluto (Greek); and the god of the underworld is called Hades (Greek). These gods are generally depicted as being eternally angry. They are also designed to be eternal in their anger. The god of the",
        " Hesperis, wife of the river god Achelous. She was the daughter of the river god, Oceanus, and the daughter of Uranus. Her mother is the sea-goddess Amphitrite, daughter of Poseidon and Mnemosyne. She"
