      "greedy_continuation": " The myth of Persephone is a story about a girl who was kidnapped by the god Hades and taken to the underworld. She was forced to stay there for nine months, but she was able to escape by eating a fig. The fig was a symbol of the goddess Demeter, who",
      "samples": [
        " Persephone is the Greek goddess of spring, and she has been a woman found in her father's garden for so long that she has come to be regarded as a constant. Her mother, Demeter, is the goddess of harvest and spring, of life and fertility. Demeter, who died",
        " Spring is the time when flowers bloom and the grass begins to green. Persephone, the goddess of the underworld, was transformed into a spring-like being known as Demeter, the goddess of agriculture. When Persephone was stolen by Hades and brought to the underworld, they",
        " Persephone is a young girl who wanders the forest, picking flowers and talking to the earth. When she hovers over the earth's branches, she falls asleep but awakens in the full spring, when flowers bloom and there is new growth.\n\nQ: Explain in your"
      ],
