      "greedy_continuation": " Milky Way. The Milky Way is a spiral galaxy, which means that it is made up of a spiral pattern of stars. The Milky Way is a spiral galaxy because it is made up of a spiral pattern of stars. The Milky Way is a spiral galaxy because it is made up of a spiral pattern",
      "samples": [
        " Milky Way. Our Sun is part of the Milky Way. The Sun and its planets are in orbit around the center of the galaxy. The Sun is rotating around the center of the galaxy.\n\nEarly astronomers thought that the Milky Way was smooth and empty. Even the sky was thought to be",
        " Milky Way, which has a radius of about 105,000 light-years. The Milky Way contains about 100 billion stars, of which 5% are bright enough to be detected with the Hubble Space Telescope. The Hubble Space Telescope has an angular resolution of about 5 arcseconds, which is equivalent to about",
        " Milky Way, which is responsible for about 98% of the universe's mass.\n\nThe Milky Way is about 4.5 billion light years in diameter. It contains about 100 billion stars, each with a mass of about ten suns.\n\nThe Milky Way's radius is about 4."
      ],
