      "greedy_continuation": " The Moon is a sphere, so it appears to change shape as it orbits the Earth. The Earth's rotation causes the Moon to appear to move in a circle, but the Moon's orbit is elliptical, so it appears to change shape as it moves around the Earth.\n\nQ: Explain",
      "samples": [
        " Because the Moon's orbit is elliptical, it is constantly being swept around its axis by a buffer of air. As it rotates, that air accretes on the Moon's surface, creating craters and mountains.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a spaceship appears to be moving",
        " It's a different shape every night. On the first night, it's flat, with a rough surface that starts out as a disk of rock, then gets thicker as it melts, then gets thinner as it cools. It's easier to see on the first night because the Moon is closer",
        " Twenty-four hours of light make the moon appear to be round in the middle, and twelve hours make it appear to be small in the middle, but the moon rises and sets along with the Sun and tides. The new moon is dependent on the tides, which change in a six-"
      ],
      "manipulation": {}
    },
