      "greedy_continuation": "\nA crab is a crab,\nAnd a crab is a crab,\nAnd a crab is a crab.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-line limerick about a crab.\nPiece:\nA crab is a crab,\nAnd a crab is a crab,\n",
      "samples": [
        "\nOnce a crab was caught in a trap,\nBut when it came out, it found a way\nOut of the trap\nThat it could not get out of.\n\nInstruction: Write a limerick about a bee.\nPiece:\nA bee keeps its honey in",
        "\nOnce on the coast, bitten by a crab,\nCrawled until the hole was to small\nTo live in the shell,\nOr carry the notch with the claw.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-line limerick about a firefly.\nPiece:",
        "\nA crab's life is a lot like that of its kin.\n\nInstruction: Write a couplet about a nut.\nPiece:\nA nut's just a nut.\n\nInstruction: Write a haunting song about a marigold.\nPiece:\n"
