      "greedy_continuation": " The long pipe is made of a softer material than the short one, so it sounds lower.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a long-distance runner can run faster than a short-distance runner.\nA: The long-distance runner's stride is longer, so he",
      "samples": [
        " Long pipes are made from a narrower tube than short pipes. The difference in the diameter of the pipes results in a more pronounced pitch, which is amplified and brings more of the sound out into the air.\n\nQ: Explain in your own words why a violin is made from a single thin",
        " When the length of a pipe is increased, it registers a higher pitch. The wind blows through the pipe at different speeds, so the pitch changes when it passes through different frequencies.\n\nQ: Which of the following elements would you use to make a song?\nA: 1. A chorus",
        " Cymbals are struck so fast that the air between them distorts the sound. If they are struck at the same speed, they produce the same sound.\n\nQ: Explain why a large bell cannot be mistaken for a small one.\nA: A bell's tone is always the"
      ],
