      "greedy_continuation": " Checkmate is when one player has a piece on the board and the other player has a piece on the board. The player who has the piece on the board has a choice of moves. If the player who has the piece on the board chooses to move, the other player can either move or check",
      "samples": [
        " In chess, checkmate is the most powerful and most effective attack. If you cannot checkmate your opponent, you cannot win. Both sides are working very hard to find ways to attack, and if they are not fighting it out they will be trapped in an endless game of 'chess' with",
        " Checkmate means that one side has won the game (the player with the white pieces [the one that starts the game]) and the other side has lost.\n\nQ: Explain by example how some people can become deaf or blind and why they have that problem.\nA: When a",
        " In chess, one player does not put the pieces on the board in any particular order. Instead, the players each start with their own pieces in their own half of the board, and checkmate is when one player turns their own pieces over to their opponent.\n\nQ: Why is it important"
      ],
