      "prompt": "Short pieces written to order.\n\nInstruction: Write a haiku about a mountain lake.\nPiece:\nCold water holding\nthe whole grey weight of the sky\nuntil wind breaks it\n\nInstruction: Write a limerick about a stubborn mule.\nPiece:\nThere once was a mule from Kilkee\nWho refused to be moved for a fee.\nHe would stand in the road,\nIgnoring his load,\nAnd nap until quarter past three.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-sentence proverb about borrowed tools.\nPiece:\nA borrowed tool comes home either broken or not at all.\n\nInstruction: Write a two-line rhyming couplet about an old clock.\nPiece:\nThe old clock keeps its argument with time,\nAnd loses, minute after patient chime.\n\nInstruction: Write a one-sentence proverb about the pawn in chess.\nPiece:",
